content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-102, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-19870, filtered-water line (chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal leakage is a steady drip of about 1 drop per second. The evidence gives no numeric leakage acceptance limit. The troubleshooting table lists shaft-seal leakage as a symptom whose corrective action is to replace the mechanical seal (5.2) and check alignment (5.4).",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration is 2.1 mm/s. The applicable limit is Figure 3 of the HF-300 manual, which classifies the highest bearing-housing reading. 2.1 mm/s falls in Zone A (0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS, 'New machines'), well below the 7.1 mm/s Zone D boundary ('Damage likely - stop the pump'). The site rule to stop immediately in the highest severity zone is not triggered. Only the drive-end reading was reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 66 C. The applicable limit is the HF-300 specification table: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C, measured on the housing surface. 66 C is within the normal band. The site requirement for a P1 work order when temperature exceeds the manufacturer's alarm limit is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall, vibration and temperature are normal, so the only defect is seal leakage. No documented stop criterion is met. The seal should be replaced as planned maintenance rather than by an emergency stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical seal faces. This is the first-listed cause of shaft-seal leakage, and it is consistent with the absence of other symptoms.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal has run dry, for example through loss of the Plan 11 flush from pump discharge. The manual states the seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. This is less likely, because vibration (Zone A) and bearing temperature (normal) give no supporting evidence, but alignment must still be checked per the corrective action.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before starting, confirm the pump serial is HF3-19870, which is below HF3-22000. The pump therefore takes component seal HF3-450 and the Table 5 torques, not service bulletin SB-2026-014.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Obtain a line-break permit and a signed lifting plan. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves, because the line is dosed with hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC. Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves. Drain and vent the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using certified lifting equipment. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the seal and shaft sleeve (HF3-455). Inspect the sleeve for scoring and record the scoring depth. Inspect the old seal faces for wear, cracking or dry-running marks to confirm the cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new component mechanical seal HF3-450, set per manual practice for pumps below HF3-22000. Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120, which must be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten all fasteners to Table 5 with lightly oiled threads: impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm, seal gland nuts M10 to 25 Nm, casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm, and bearing housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm if disturbed. Do not use the 30 Nm bulletin value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. Tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is in place and the casing is full. Never run the seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, check the seal for leakage. Measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading against Figure 3. Confirm bearing housing temperature is below 70 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Mechanical seal, component type. This is the correct seal for serial HF3-19870, which is below HF3-22000.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, which must be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. This is a contingency spare, fitted only if inspection finds unacceptable scoring.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Line-break permit; drain and vent before opening the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, which exceeds 25 kg. A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-102 is on a line dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not run the pump dry. The Plan 11 flush must be established before start-up.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment check: 1.5 h with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The seal part and gland nut torque differ between sources. Manual Table 5 and the parts list specify seal HF3-450 with gland nuts at 25 Nm. Service bulletin SB-2026-014 (14 March 2026) specifies cartridge seal HF3-450B at 30 Nm. The bulletin applies only to serial HF3-22000 and above, and it explicitly states that pumps below HF3-22000 continue to use HF3-450 and Table 5. P-102 is serial HF3-19870, so the manual applies: HF3-450 with gland nuts at 25 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bulletin's sleeve replacement criterion (replace HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm) is written for pumps at serial HF3-22000 and above. It does not formally apply to HF3-19870, and the manual only says to inspect for scoring without giving a limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "No documented acceptable seal leakage rate exists, so the evidence cannot say how urgent a 1 drop per second leak is beyond planned replacement.",
    "There is no sleeve scoring rejection limit for pumps below serial HF3-22000; the manual gives none. Engineering must confirm whether the bulletin's 0.1 mm criterion may be used as guidance.",
    "Only the drive-end vibration was reported. The non-drive-end reading is needed, because the classification uses the highest reading on both housings.",
    "Seal faces are not a separate part in the evidence. It is not stated whether HF3-450 includes all seal hardware.",
    "It is not known whether the Plan 11 flush was interrupted or the seal ran dry. Operating history should be checked to confirm the cause.",
    "Spare part availability and lead time for HF3-450, HF3-120 and HF3-455 are not covered by the evidence."
  ]
}
